WEBVTT

00:01.620 --> 00:04.659
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:04.727 --> 00:07.748
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:07.816 --> 00:11.206
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.273 --> 00:14.161
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:14.245 --> 00:17.785
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.836 --> 00:21.009
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.093 --> 00:22.662
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:22.729 --> 00:24.032
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:24.099 --> 00:27.188
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:39.461 --> 00:40.713
Trick or treat?!

00:40.781 --> 00:43.119
Chris, what in God's name
are you doing?

00:43.187 --> 00:44.955
Y-You can't go out
dressed like that.

00:45.024 --> 00:46.892
Why not? I'm Bill Cosby.

00:46.961 --> 00:50.466
Okay, but, I mean,
y-you can't go out like that.

00:50.534 --> 00:52.838
Well, come on, Mom,
don't I look like him?

00:52.906 --> 00:56.196
(imitating Bill Cosby
with slurred mumbling)

00:56.264 --> 00:59.769
Well, yes, but, Chris, you can't
just walk around in blackface.

00:59.837 --> 01:00.905
It's racist.

01:00.972 --> 01:02.408
Now, go upstairs and put on

01:02.476 --> 01:04.345
that Indian chief costume
I bought you.

01:04.413 --> 01:06.049
Aw, I don't want to!

01:06.117 --> 01:09.423
(slurred muttering)

01:16.455 --> 01:18.308
Peter, what's with
all the eggs?

01:18.375 --> 01:20.528
Oh, well, every Halloween,
me, Joe and Quagmire

01:20.596 --> 01:22.300
do this thing where
one of us is it,

01:22.368 --> 01:23.652
and then the
other two of us

01:23.720 --> 01:25.456
nail the crap out of him
with awesome pranks.

01:25.524 --> 01:27.125
Well, who's it this year?

01:40.438 --> 01:41.272
Damn it.

01:47.419 --> 01:48.287
(gasps)

01:49.657 --> 01:51.710
(screaming)

01:51.795 --> 01:53.096
Guys, guys, be careful!

01:53.164 --> 01:54.599
This isn't my box!

01:54.667 --> 01:56.303
Oh, yeah, sure.
Then whose is it?

01:56.371 --> 01:57.639
MAN:
It's mine.

01:57.707 --> 01:59.693
I'm Dick Pump,
and I'd appreciate it

01:59.761 --> 02:02.800
if you hooligans didn't get
your eggs all over my parcel.

02:02.868 --> 02:04.436
Sorry. I keep getting
your mail, Dick.

02:04.504 --> 02:05.705
Hey, what's in there, anyway?

02:05.773 --> 02:07.276
Embarrassing stuff.

02:13.489 --> 02:16.161
Wow, that was
terrific, Jessica.

02:16.228 --> 02:18.014
It was good for me, too.

02:18.082 --> 02:19.317
(screams)

02:19.384 --> 02:20.286
(laughing)

02:20.354 --> 02:22.407
Got-got you again, Quagmire.

02:22.475 --> 02:24.344
You said you were that
waitress from Friendly's!

02:24.412 --> 02:26.082
I lied.
You jerk!

02:26.149 --> 02:27.684
I didn't feel anything.

02:27.752 --> 02:28.837
But you did!

02:28.905 --> 02:31.442
Happy Halloween,
(bleep).

02:33.580 --> 02:35.184
Hey, hey, get away!

02:35.251 --> 02:36.452
Just get away
from me, Peter!

02:36.521 --> 02:37.856
Hey, take it easy, Quagmire.

02:37.923 --> 02:39.159
Nobody wants to hurt you.

02:39.226 --> 02:40.093
Right, Joe?

02:41.263 --> 02:42.665
Gotcha!

02:42.733 --> 02:44.169
Ha! Hepatitis-C!

02:44.236 --> 02:45.856
Joke's on you;
I already got it.

02:45.923 --> 02:47.492
Meningitis!

02:47.560 --> 02:48.495
I'm a carrier.

02:48.562 --> 02:49.513
Gonorrhea!

02:49.581 --> 02:50.665
Patient Zero.

02:50.733 --> 02:52.386
You're gonna have to do
better than that.

02:53.806 --> 02:54.858
I don't know, Joe.
That's it.

02:54.926 --> 02:56.511
We're out of known diseases.

02:56.578 --> 02:57.946
Unless...

03:21.062 --> 03:24.252
All right, what this is has
no name, so you can't have it.

03:24.319 --> 03:26.489
(mosquito buzzing)

03:30.398 --> 03:31.866
(chuckles)

03:31.935 --> 03:32.869
We got him.

03:32.937 --> 03:34.806
Halloween is fun.

03:38.181 --> 03:40.385
What was that?

03:47.818 --> 03:49.036
(gasps)
Oh, my God.

03:49.103 --> 03:50.406
I knew this day would come.

03:50.473 --> 03:52.310
Rupert, we're under attack
by monsters!

03:52.377 --> 03:53.579
Dear God!

03:53.646 --> 03:54.848
Oh, but wait, there's Superman.

03:54.916 --> 03:55.916
He'll save us.

03:55.984 --> 03:57.620
Superman! Superman!

03:57.688 --> 03:59.291
Wait, wait.
Where are you going?!

03:59.359 --> 04:00.644
Ah, to hell with him.

04:00.728 --> 04:02.296
We'll have to deal with
these marauders ourselves.

04:02.364 --> 04:03.600
Rupert, man your station.

04:05.471 --> 04:09.295
All right, you undead bastards,
time to send you back to hell!

04:09.362 --> 04:12.000
(Stewie yelling, kids screaming)

04:15.491 --> 04:17.427
Hey, Stewie, you all set
to go trick-or-treating?

04:17.495 --> 04:18.965
Whoa, what the hell
are you doing?!

04:19.016 --> 04:20.501
We're under attack, Brian!

04:20.569 --> 04:23.107
By zombies and vampires
and a Mexican princess!

04:23.174 --> 04:24.844
Stewie, those aren't monsters,
they're kids.

04:24.911 --> 04:25.945
They're trick-or-treaters.

04:26.014 --> 04:28.117
Trick-or-treaters?

04:28.184 --> 04:29.987
Yeah. It's what kids do
on Halloween.

04:30.055 --> 04:31.290
They-they dress up
in costumes,

04:31.342 --> 04:32.943
and they go around
asking for candy.

04:33.011 --> 04:34.714
How do you not know
about trick-or-treating?

04:34.781 --> 04:36.718
Well, how do you not know
that your reflection

04:36.785 --> 04:38.556
in the patio door
isn't another dog?

04:38.622 --> 04:40.792
Hey! That guy is a dick.

04:41.963 --> 04:42.998
Hey, get out of here!

04:43.065 --> 04:44.784
This is my house!

04:44.836 --> 04:46.020
Oh, my God, Brian.

04:46.088 --> 04:47.023
What happened?

04:47.091 --> 04:48.359
Who did this to you?

04:48.427 --> 04:49.427
Did you do this?!

04:49.495 --> 04:50.697
You son of a bitch!

04:57.178 --> 04:58.429
Okay, see you
later, Mom.

04:58.497 --> 05:00.299
Oh, where are you
off to, sweetie?

05:00.367 --> 05:02.320
You gonna go see
three movies in a row

05:02.387 --> 05:04.242
so it seems like
you're out doing something?

05:04.309 --> 05:07.681
No, Mom. I'm going to my first
big high school Halloween party.

05:07.750 --> 05:09.152
Oh, that's nice.

05:09.219 --> 05:10.488
What are you dressed as?

05:10.556 --> 05:11.857
I'm a slutty cat.

05:11.925 --> 05:13.393
I'll be back late.
Don't wait up.

05:15.582 --> 05:17.335
Quack, quack.

05:17.402 --> 05:19.990
Oh! My little ducky.

05:20.058 --> 05:22.162
You look so adorable.

05:22.230 --> 05:23.732
Oh, no, no.
You see these holes?

05:23.800 --> 05:25.185
I got bit by a vampire.

05:25.252 --> 05:26.554
I'm a vampire duck.

05:26.622 --> 05:28.692
But I'm a modern vampire duck
who hangs around

05:28.760 --> 05:31.181
with Anna Paquin and drives
around in a black Mercedes.

05:31.249 --> 05:32.300
What is that?

05:32.367 --> 05:33.469
<i>It's True Blood.</i>

05:33.536 --> 05:34.938
Yeah, no one knows
what that is.

05:35.005 --> 05:36.642
Rich, gay people do.

05:42.940 --> 05:45.994
Brian, are you sure
none of these are real monsters?

05:46.078 --> 05:47.247
Stewie, it's
gonna be fine.

05:47.315 --> 05:48.566
Look, here's
our first house.

05:48.634 --> 05:50.002
There you go.

05:50.087 --> 05:53.761
A Cornish game hen for you,
a Cornish game hen for you.

05:53.829 --> 05:56.099
Everybody gets a hen.

05:56.166 --> 05:58.103
Would you like
some gravy?

05:58.171 --> 06:00.608
Sure you'd like
some gravy.

06:02.396 --> 06:04.500
Oh, my God, Brian,
you were right.

06:04.568 --> 06:05.736
Halloween is
the best.

06:05.820 --> 06:07.372
Look how much candy I have.

06:07.456 --> 06:08.691
Oh, w-where should we go next?

06:08.743 --> 06:10.211
Ooh, look, there's Mort's house.

06:10.296 --> 06:12.532
Oh, but I hope he doesn't have
some gross Jewish candy,

06:12.584 --> 06:14.837
like-like Rugelach
or-or Hamentashen

06:14.889 --> 06:17.059
or-or Hachahachahacha.

06:17.143 --> 06:18.211
R-Right, Brian?

06:18.262 --> 06:19.431
Brian?

06:19.499 --> 06:20.566
Brian, where are you?

06:23.407 --> 06:25.693
Hey, kid,
nice costume.

06:25.761 --> 06:26.695
Really?

06:26.763 --> 06:28.132
Oh, my God, thank you so much.

06:28.200 --> 06:29.969
My mother bought it for me,
and I was worried

06:30.037 --> 06:32.240
it might be a tad banal,
but if you big kids like it,

06:32.308 --> 06:33.476
then it must be pretty cool.

06:33.543 --> 06:35.948
That's a nice bag
of candy you've got.

06:36.016 --> 06:37.133
Oh, thank you.

06:37.201 --> 06:38.604
You know, it's actually
a pillowcase.

06:38.671 --> 06:40.557
Th-They're sort of thrifty
around my house, you know.

06:40.625 --> 06:41.960
Well, now it's ours.

06:42.028 --> 06:43.163
Uh, well, no.

06:43.231 --> 06:44.249
But how about this?

06:44.316 --> 06:46.753
You can have the apple
and the raisins

06:46.822 --> 06:49.092
and the cheese and crackers
with the little red stick.

06:49.159 --> 06:51.246
I don't, I don't know
how that's candy, but...

06:52.416 --> 06:53.501
Thanks, duck boy.

06:53.569 --> 06:54.903
(laughter)

06:59.631 --> 07:00.616
Hey, get back here!

07:00.684 --> 07:02.035
Hey, that's my candy!

07:02.103 --> 07:04.424
Damn you, that's my candy!

07:04.492 --> 07:06.762
Oh, how could this day
get any worse?

07:06.829 --> 07:08.014
(mosquito buzzing)

07:09.085 --> 07:10.819
(screams)

07:16.145 --> 07:18.515
Brian! Brian, help me! Brian!

07:18.599 --> 07:19.551
Hey, there you are.

07:19.636 --> 07:20.870
Brian, where were you?

07:20.938 --> 07:22.774
Well, that jerk dog
from our patio door

07:22.842 --> 07:24.344
somehow got inside a hubcap.

07:24.412 --> 07:26.115
I just wanted to alert
the owner of the car.

07:26.182 --> 07:27.300
I left a note
on his windshield.

07:27.368 --> 07:28.486
Wh-What is wrong with you?

07:28.554 --> 07:29.956
You abandoned me!

07:30.024 --> 07:32.327
And some larger
children took my candy.

07:32.395 --> 07:33.596
Al-All right, look,
just calm down.

07:33.664 --> 07:34.599
It's still early.

07:34.667 --> 07:35.768
We'll get you more candy.

07:39.593 --> 07:40.894
Brian, this
isn't working.

07:40.980 --> 07:42.933
What do you want me
to do, Stewie? It's late.

07:43.017 --> 07:44.719
Everybody's stopped
giving out candy.

07:44.787 --> 07:46.656
Well, then let's get
my candy back, Brian.

07:46.724 --> 07:48.995
Let's track down the punks who
stole it and make them pay.

07:49.063 --> 07:50.131
Look, Stewie,
I don't think that...

07:50.199 --> 07:51.634
Brian, please.

07:51.702 --> 07:54.006
This is my first Halloween,
and-and it's ruined.

07:54.074 --> 07:55.341
(sighs)
All right, all right, fine.

07:55.409 --> 07:56.377
We'll look for them.

07:56.445 --> 07:58.014
Good, because so far,

07:58.082 --> 08:00.920
Halloween's a bigger letdown
than being a Mets fan.

08:00.987 --> 08:02.757
ANNOUNCER:
Opening day, and here's
the first pitch.

08:02.825 --> 08:03.725
(bat cracks)

08:03.793 --> 08:05.863
And the season's over.

08:09.438 --> 08:11.975
Ah, you were a good sport
this year, Quagmire.

08:12.043 --> 08:14.380
Ah, well, you know, Peter,
it's all in good fun, right?

08:14.448 --> 08:16.318
You know, my grandfather
used to have a saying...

08:16.385 --> 08:18.223
(speaking Japanese)

08:22.666 --> 08:24.468
Holy crap, you speak Ebonics?

08:24.536 --> 08:26.005
No, no, Peter,
it's Japanese.

08:26.073 --> 08:28.076
Wait, are they,
are they the angry eye ones

08:28.144 --> 08:29.946
or the tired eye ones?

08:30.014 --> 08:32.452
Uh, I-I'm not
sure I underst--

08:32.520 --> 08:33.653
Uh, the first
one, I guess.

08:33.722 --> 08:35.024
I-I don't know.

08:35.092 --> 08:37.362
M-My grandfather on my
mom's side was Japanese.

08:37.429 --> 08:39.366
Wait a minute,
you're-you're part Japanese?

08:39.433 --> 08:40.434
Sure am.

08:40.502 --> 08:41.838
My grandfather
was a pilot

08:41.906 --> 08:44.042
for the Imperial Air Force
during World War Two.

08:44.110 --> 08:46.413
Flew a kamikaze mission
in the Battle of Midway.

08:46.481 --> 08:48.351
He's part of the reason
I became a pilot.

08:48.419 --> 08:50.355
Wow. How come
I never met him?

08:50.423 --> 08:51.624
He was a
kamikaze pilot.

08:51.692 --> 08:53.595
Yeah, no, I heard you,
he was a Karma Chameleon,

08:53.663 --> 08:55.265
but how-how come
I never met him?

08:55.333 --> 08:56.367
Because he
died, Peter.

08:56.435 --> 08:57.803
Oh, my God, when?

08:57.872 --> 08:58.990
And how?

09:01.129 --> 09:03.014
Hey, Joe,
what are you doing?

09:03.066 --> 09:05.103
I thought we were gonna go
to The Clam and get wasted.

09:05.171 --> 09:06.104
Ugh, I can't.

09:06.172 --> 09:07.107
I'm on duty tonight.

09:07.175 --> 09:08.376
And Halloween's got to be

09:08.443 --> 09:10.112
the worst night of the year
to be a cop.

09:10.180 --> 09:13.520
All you do is drive around,
confiscate beer from teenagers

09:13.588 --> 09:16.692
and occasionally handcuff
a drunk woman in a sexy costume.

09:16.761 --> 09:17.812
Aw, cool!

09:17.880 --> 09:19.047
Hey, I got a great idea.

09:19.115 --> 09:20.317
How about
we ride around with you

09:20.385 --> 09:21.753
and steal beer from teenagers?

09:21.821 --> 09:23.323
I don't know, you guys.

09:23.391 --> 09:25.578
This is my job, and I can't
have you fooling around,

09:25.645 --> 09:26.781
getting into trouble.

09:26.848 --> 09:28.785
Hey, when the hell
do I get into trouble?

09:28.852 --> 09:31.490
Well, didn't you get lost
in the grocery store last week?

09:31.558 --> 09:33.428
(wailing)

09:36.635 --> 09:38.504
Are you okay?
No!

09:38.572 --> 09:41.945
I came in with my wife
and now I can't find her!

09:42.013 --> 09:43.983
Oh, I'm sure
she's here somewhere.

09:44.050 --> 09:45.536
Come on,
I'll help you find her.

09:45.604 --> 09:47.339
Okay.

09:47.408 --> 09:50.379
(over P.A.):
Will Lois Griffin please
come to the courtesy booth.

09:50.447 --> 09:51.966
We have a little
gift for you.

09:52.034 --> 09:53.920
(giggles)

09:53.988 --> 09:56.174
I'm Lois-- Oh, for
God's sakes, Peter.

09:56.259 --> 09:57.911
Yay, Lois!

10:01.103 --> 10:02.905
This is so cool.

10:02.973 --> 10:04.475
Our first high school
Halloween party.

10:04.543 --> 10:06.178
Do you think
we'll get to make out?

10:06.245 --> 10:08.700
These things always end up
in make out sessions.

10:08.768 --> 10:10.103
Hey, you know what,
you guys?

10:10.171 --> 10:11.740
My cousin went to
a Halloween party

10:11.808 --> 10:13.410
and made out with a guy,
and she's hideous.

10:13.478 --> 10:14.980
I mean, really hideous.

10:15.048 --> 10:16.083
How'd your cousin
do it?

10:16.151 --> 10:17.936
She wore a mask.
Don't you get it?

10:18.004 --> 10:20.041
If we wear our masks
and we don't take them off

10:20.109 --> 10:22.395
for the whole party, the
boys won't know who we are,

10:22.463 --> 10:24.132
and we'll have a better
chance of hooking up.

10:24.200 --> 10:25.252
Good idea!

10:25.320 --> 10:26.503
We are so
gonna hook up!

10:26.572 --> 10:27.540
I think we look hot.

10:27.624 --> 10:28.658
Totally hot.

10:28.710 --> 10:30.094
Ugly bitches!

10:30.162 --> 10:31.849
Moo!

10:34.054 --> 10:35.406
JOE:
So what's the story, Quagmire?

10:35.473 --> 10:38.512
Do you observe any particular
Japanese customs?

10:38.579 --> 10:40.632
QUAGMIRE:
Oh, yeah, I'm very in
touch with my Asian roots.

10:40.700 --> 10:43.021
You notice I take my shoes off
whenever I enter my house.

10:43.089 --> 10:44.525
PETER:
Oh, yeah.

10:44.592 --> 10:46.428
I do five hours of math
homework every night

10:46.480 --> 10:47.781
even though I'm
no longer in school.

10:47.865 --> 10:49.034
Ah.

10:49.102 --> 10:50.603
Sometimes I drink
out of a wooden box.

10:50.655 --> 10:52.440
Ooh.
Ah, very Asian.

10:52.492 --> 10:54.712
I was a very cute baby and
now I'm a joyless adult.

10:54.780 --> 10:56.633
Ah.
They are unhappy.

10:56.717 --> 10:59.974
DISPATCHER:
All units, we've got a domestic
disturbance at Fifth and Maple.

11:00.040 --> 11:03.063
This is Officer Swanson
responding, I'm on my way.

11:03.131 --> 11:05.601
All right you guys, these
domestic dispute situations

11:05.670 --> 11:08.458
can get pretty dicey, so I need
you to stay in the car, okay?

11:08.526 --> 11:09.994
No joking around.

11:11.832 --> 11:13.985
All right, sir, sir, ma'am.
I just need you to tell me

11:14.053 --> 11:14.955
clearly and calmly,
what happened.

11:15.022 --> 11:16.942
One at a time, please.

11:17.010 --> 11:19.547
This whore gets her stubby little
fingers into my wallet! That's larceny!

11:19.631 --> 11:22.352
He puts one of those cigars in his mouth
and he turns into a different person!

11:22.420 --> 11:23.722
PETER:
No freakin' way.

11:23.789 --> 11:25.693
Guys, I told you
to wait in the car.

11:25.761 --> 11:28.482
Domestic abuse is a
very delicate matter.

11:28.550 --> 11:31.405
Joe, this isn't domestic
abuse, this is hilarious.

11:31.473 --> 11:32.941
And another thing--

11:33.009 --> 11:34.744
I'm tired of massaging
your foot knuckles!

11:34.812 --> 11:37.902
You call that a massage,
with your baby carrot fingers?!

11:37.969 --> 11:39.037
Go to hell!
Come here!

11:39.105 --> 11:40.407
Get over here!

11:40.475 --> 11:42.511
Stay away from me!
You keep him away from me!

11:42.562 --> 11:44.215
You little...!

11:44.266 --> 11:45.501
(both yelling)

11:45.568 --> 11:46.737
Get over here!

11:46.821 --> 11:48.741
I'm gonna jump over you
and I'm gonna... !

11:48.825 --> 11:49.926
Come back here!

11:49.994 --> 11:51.280
All right, that's
enough, you two.

11:51.364 --> 11:52.397
This is serious. Stop it.

11:52.449 --> 11:54.570
(all yelling)

11:54.637 --> 11:57.927
Oh, quick, Quagmire,
give me your iPod.

11:58.011 --> 12:00.882
(comedic, carnival-like music
playing; yelling continues)

12:00.950 --> 12:02.769
WOMAN:
I swear to God!

12:02.853 --> 12:04.723
You keep him away from me!

12:06.279 --> 12:08.064
JOE:
Got 'em.

12:09.618 --> 12:10.904
Aw, they got tuckered out.

12:10.972 --> 12:13.341
Of course they did, they ran
like two miles for them.

12:18.052 --> 12:19.388
Okay, there they are, Brian.

12:19.456 --> 12:21.325
And they've still got my candy.

12:21.393 --> 12:23.796
You distract them, and I'll run
up from behind and grab it.

12:23.865 --> 12:25.065
Stewie, don't be ridiculous.

12:25.133 --> 12:27.120
They're kids,
and I'm an adult.

12:27.188 --> 12:29.943
I'll just go over there and calmly
ask them to give back the candy.

12:30.011 --> 12:31.645
Hi, fellas.

12:31.698 --> 12:33.751
Hey, look,
it's Snoopy.

12:33.818 --> 12:35.821
Hey, Snoopy,
where's Woodstock?

12:35.889 --> 12:37.859
Ah, that-- that's a good one.

12:37.926 --> 12:40.197
Uh, listen, my friend,
Stewie, he's just a baby,

12:40.265 --> 12:41.900
and you guys took
his candy earlier.

12:41.968 --> 12:43.904
What do you say
you just give it back,

12:43.972 --> 12:45.341
and we all forget
this ever happened?

12:45.410 --> 12:46.643
Sure, why not?

12:46.712 --> 12:48.414
Your friend's candy is
right around the corner.

12:48.481 --> 12:49.734
All right. Terrific.

12:54.695 --> 12:56.030
Hey, hey, what are you doing?

12:56.098 --> 12:57.098
Stop it!
(spray can hissing)

12:57.167 --> 12:58.469
Hey, let me go! No! No!

12:58.537 --> 12:59.704
(Brian screaming)

13:02.210 --> 13:04.614
Oh my God, you
look so cute.

13:04.682 --> 13:06.268
What is that, spray paint?

13:06.336 --> 13:07.754
Yeah. Those little
punks want a war.

13:07.822 --> 13:09.124
And now they've got one.

13:09.192 --> 13:11.561
Hey, here's someone who
might understand how you feel.

13:13.733 --> 13:16.472
Hey, how you doing.
First day being pink?

13:16.539 --> 13:17.675
Yeah.

13:17.743 --> 13:19.177
Welcome to hell.

13:19.245 --> 13:22.885
(dramatic musical sting)

13:29.076 --> 13:30.911
All right, Brian,
we're getting my candy back,

13:30.979 --> 13:32.666
and here's how
it's gonna go down:

13:32.751 --> 13:35.122
First, we track down those teenage
hoodlums and kill them all.

13:35.173 --> 13:36.758
Yeah, okay, fine,
let's kill 'em.

13:36.825 --> 13:39.363
Wha-- really? No way.

13:39.431 --> 13:41.217
No, I was only half serious.

13:41.285 --> 13:43.121
We can't do that.

13:43.189 --> 13:45.910
Oh, my God-- Pink Brian
is crazy Brian.

13:45.977 --> 13:47.447
Oh, man.

13:47.515 --> 13:49.183
I know, I know we can't.

13:49.251 --> 13:51.004
I just feel bad they
stole your candy.

13:51.071 --> 13:53.809
Well, now I know how Peter feels
when Mort steals his paper.

13:57.385 --> 14:00.424
Come on, that's right,
you bastard.

14:02.362 --> 14:03.329
Stop right there!

14:05.401 --> 14:07.038
Give me the paper!

14:07.105 --> 14:09.125
No! No! Don't hurt me,
you bastard.

14:09.193 --> 14:11.012
Mort, give me the paper.

14:11.080 --> 14:12.916
No, I'm reading it in here.

14:12.984 --> 14:14.619
You can have the
real estate section.

14:14.688 --> 14:15.990
It's for schmucks, anyway.

14:23.605 --> 14:25.375
Okay, your turn
to spin the bottle,

14:25.443 --> 14:27.279
guy dressed like Bill Clinton.

14:27.346 --> 14:29.283
(chuckles)
Yeah, dressed like.

14:35.163 --> 14:37.734
All right, let's go make
some Whitewater.

14:43.029 --> 14:45.550
Okay, Slutty Cat,
you're up next.

14:45.618 --> 14:47.488
Oh my God, this is
totally working.

14:47.555 --> 14:49.190
Nobody knows who we are.

14:54.787 --> 14:57.691
All right. Slutty Cat
and Optimus Prime.

14:57.760 --> 14:58.961
Into the closet.

14:59.030 --> 15:01.033
(giggling)

15:01.100 --> 15:03.621
Oh, my God, you're
gonna hook up.

15:03.688 --> 15:04.656
With a boy.

15:04.724 --> 15:06.794
I know. I can't believe it.

15:06.862 --> 15:09.500
Oh, I feel as pretty
as Scarlett Johansson.

15:09.568 --> 15:11.320
PHOTOGRAPHERS:
Scarlett!
Scarlett Johansson!

15:11.387 --> 15:13.742
Scarlett Johansson! Scarlett!
Scarlett Johansson!

15:13.826 --> 15:14.593
Scarlett!
Scarlett!

15:16.398 --> 15:17.666
Laura Linney.

15:19.805 --> 15:21.106
Whoops.

15:21.174 --> 15:22.711
(kissing sounds)

15:22.778 --> 15:24.130
Come on, you guys.

15:24.198 --> 15:25.800
It's been well
over seven minutes.

15:25.868 --> 15:27.153
(passionate moaning)

15:27.221 --> 15:28.288
Let's go.

15:28.357 --> 15:30.910
Other people want
to use the closet.

15:30.979 --> 15:32.162
You guys...

15:32.230 --> 15:33.466
(gasps)

15:33.534 --> 15:35.871
Oh.... my... God.

15:40.414 --> 15:41.616
Chris?

15:41.684 --> 15:42.802
Meg?

15:42.886 --> 15:45.691
(screaming)
(screaming)

15:45.759 --> 15:47.795
Oh, my God, what are
you doing here?!

15:47.863 --> 15:49.131
Trying to grab some boob!

15:49.198 --> 15:50.284
From your sister?!

15:50.352 --> 15:51.837
I didn't know it was you!

15:51.905 --> 15:53.640
Well, who did you think it was?!

15:53.708 --> 15:55.311
Some bitch! Who cares?!

15:55.378 --> 15:56.581
(retching)

15:56.648 --> 15:58.283
Oh, my God!

15:58.352 --> 15:59.720
Oh. We did so much!

15:59.788 --> 16:01.540
Shut up! Shut up! Shut up!

16:01.609 --> 16:03.461
We're disgusting!

16:03.529 --> 16:05.766
We're a disgrace
to our family!

16:05.834 --> 16:08.338
Oh, maybe I can
get in on this.

16:14.085 --> 16:17.055
Oh, it's good to finally
be off duty.

16:17.123 --> 16:19.929
Wow, I never knew about
this place, Quagmire.

16:19.996 --> 16:22.133
Yeah, this is
the Air Force graveyard,

16:22.201 --> 16:24.237
where old military planes
come to die.

16:24.305 --> 16:25.724
That one over there
is my favorite.

16:25.792 --> 16:27.828
It's an old Japanese Zero.

16:27.896 --> 16:30.334
Wow, no calories and all
that Japanese taste?

16:30.401 --> 16:31.870
That's the kind of plane

16:31.937 --> 16:33.824
my grandfather used to
fly in the war. Cool.

16:35.763 --> 16:39.168
Man, this thing looks like it
still might be in working order.

16:45.566 --> 16:47.134
You guys want to go for a ride?

16:47.202 --> 16:48.521
Ah, sure.
Hell, yeah.

16:51.027 --> 16:54.099
Wow, I always thought the
Japanese flew flying saucers.

17:17.448 --> 17:19.418
All right, there they are.

17:19.486 --> 17:21.522
All right, boys,
it's candy time.

17:21.590 --> 17:22.692
Let's dig in.

17:28.922 --> 17:30.808
Okay, Brian, let's do this.

17:30.876 --> 17:32.044
Give me a boost.

17:36.488 --> 17:37.989
Hello.

17:40.263 --> 17:42.483
Hey, it's that stupid kid.

17:42.550 --> 17:44.286
Yes, it's that stupid kid.

17:44.354 --> 17:46.692
Now, listen very closely, 'cause
here's how it's gonna go down.

17:54.241 --> 17:55.878
(roaring)

18:00.554 --> 18:02.674
(cheering)

18:02.741 --> 18:04.912
Guys, guys, guys,

18:04.980 --> 18:07.985
I don't want to toot my own horn
here, but I think that was me.

18:10.943 --> 18:12.077
(yells)

18:13.982 --> 18:17.489
Well, there's only one thing
to do now: go to plan B.

18:17.556 --> 18:20.444
Mom!

18:22.082 --> 18:24.553
I am so sorry, Mrs. Griffin.

18:24.621 --> 18:26.774
I have no idea what
got into my son.

18:26.841 --> 18:29.847
Well, just have him return
the candy and everything's fine.

18:29.915 --> 18:34.958
Justin, you give this young man
his candy back, right now.

18:35.042 --> 18:36.444
All right, here.

18:37.614 --> 18:39.017
Thanks.

18:39.083 --> 18:40.720
Now, we want Justin's candy.

18:40.788 --> 18:41.671
What?

18:41.739 --> 18:43.075
You heard me.

18:43.142 --> 18:45.112
Take Justin's bag of candy
and pour it into Stewie's.

18:45.180 --> 18:46.348
All of it.

18:46.432 --> 18:48.151
And if I think you're
holding back on me,

18:48.236 --> 18:49.538
we're gonna have
a serious problem.

18:49.606 --> 18:50.941
Well, all right.

18:51.008 --> 18:52.376
That's what I'm talking about.

18:52.445 --> 18:53.646
Yeah, serious problem.

18:56.019 --> 18:57.655
Good. Now, go in your purse,

18:57.723 --> 18:59.826
take out $40
and put it in the bag.

18:59.894 --> 19:02.265
All right, Lois, you're
kind of scaring me now.

19:02.332 --> 19:04.536
I-I-I don't have $40.

19:04.603 --> 19:06.623
All right, I understand.

19:06.691 --> 19:08.979
I'll be back tomorrow
for the $80.

19:09.046 --> 19:10.849
And I'm taking
your welcome mat.

19:20.753 --> 19:24.093
Whoa, Quahog looks
beautiful from up here.

19:24.161 --> 19:25.897
Yeah, this thing handles
pretty smooth, doesn't it?

19:25.964 --> 19:27.817
Feels right.

19:27.885 --> 19:30.490
Feels kind of like something
I was meant to fly, you know.

19:30.557 --> 19:31.692
Hey, there's Quahog Harbor.

19:33.630 --> 19:36.118
Look at all those
old naval vessels.

19:36.202 --> 19:38.089
Yeah, look at 'em all.

19:40.912 --> 19:42.848
Whoa, whoa, easy, Quagmire.
What are you doing?

19:42.916 --> 19:44.451
I don't know, Peter.

19:44.519 --> 19:46.856
It's like something just
awakened inside me.

19:46.924 --> 19:49.379
I can feel my grandfather's
Japanese blood

19:49.446 --> 19:50.614
coursing through my veins.

19:56.210 --> 19:57.578
Quagmire, what the hell's
the matter with you?

19:57.630 --> 19:58.714
What are you nuts?

19:58.782 --> 19:59.750
Shut up, roundeye!

20:02.590 --> 20:05.310
Oh, my God! Stop, Quagmire!
I don't want to die.

20:05.378 --> 20:06.514
Please don't kill us!

20:06.598 --> 20:11.907
(shouting in Japanese)

20:11.976 --> 20:13.645
<i>Banzai!</i>

20:13.696 --> 20:15.616
Oh, God!
No!

20:18.455 --> 20:20.492
(screaming)

20:20.544 --> 20:22.213
You know what they call this
in my country?

20:22.297 --> 20:23.665
What?! What?!
Payback.

20:32.402 --> 20:34.823
(panting):
What the hell was that?

20:34.891 --> 20:36.877
Prank's on
you, (bleep).

20:36.945 --> 20:38.196
I'm not Japanese.

20:38.264 --> 20:39.949
You're not?
No.

20:40.017 --> 20:42.589
That was for making me have sex
with Joe, you sons of bitches.

20:42.673 --> 20:44.643
You guys actually had sex?

20:44.710 --> 20:46.864
Yeah, I kind of went
rogue with that one.

20:53.041 --> 20:55.144
Brian, you took me out on my
first Halloween tonight,

20:55.212 --> 20:57.015
and you showed me
an exciting time.

20:57.083 --> 20:59.153
And for that,
I'm going to let you

20:59.220 --> 21:01.157
pick out some candy from my bag.
Oh, thanks.

21:01.225 --> 21:03.712
And keep in mind, we can't use
any actual brand names

21:03.780 --> 21:05.550
due to advertising concerns.

21:05.618 --> 21:08.288
Right, okay, I'll have
a Mr. Whip-o Bar,

21:08.356 --> 21:09.592
a Kooky Nut Pop,

21:09.659 --> 21:11.061
some Jim 'n M's,

21:11.128 --> 21:12.965
uh, a Zip Zap,

21:13.032 --> 21:14.400
a Choco Buddy,

21:14.468 --> 21:16.772
uh, a Sixty-Four-
Thousand-Dollar Bar,

21:16.840 --> 21:18.343
a Notafinger

21:18.410 --> 21:20.013
and a Dawkin's
Peanut Butter Disc.

21:20.081 --> 21:21.682
God, I hate television.

21:23.153 --> 21:25.190
Brian, why are you pink?

21:25.258 --> 21:26.560
(sniffs)

21:26.628 --> 21:28.564
Why do you and Meg smell
like sweat and shame?

21:28.632 --> 21:32.305
Uh, well... you see,
um... we, uh...

21:32.373 --> 21:34.526
You know what?
I don't care.

21:34.593 --> 21:36.580
I hooked up with
a chick tonight,

21:36.648 --> 21:38.752
and I am pretty darn
proud of myself.

21:38.819 --> 21:40.454
You're right, Chris.

21:40.522 --> 21:42.259
I hooked up
with a guy tonight--

21:42.326 --> 21:43.395
a high school guy--

21:43.462 --> 21:45.432
and I think maybe
he'll call tomorrow.

21:45.500 --> 21:48.104
You may be disappointed.

21:48.105 --> 22:49.105
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru